From 92d1686de39a5d111c0bdc6b33d85f3f2bbc624d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shkosugi <sin.kosugi@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 16:29:27 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] LINQ to SQL: System.Data.Linq ported from referencesource

The sources of Microsoft's referencesource (MIT), compiled for .NET as WebFormsForCore.Data.Linq
(assembly System.Data.Linq, its original ECMA identity). Changes for .NET, all under Core\ or #if:
- Core\Strings.generated.cs, Core\Error.generated.cs: referencesource has only part of the resource
  text (System.Data.Linq.txt); generated from .NET Framework 4.8's own assembly (its resources for
  the format strings, invoking each Error method for its exception type), by
  experiments/wf4c/generate-dlinq-resources.ps1 of the FrameworkOnCore repository.
- Core\SecurityUtils.cs replaces misc\SecurityUtils.cs (Code Access Security demands; .NET runs
  fully trusted), Core\ThisAssembly.cs the build-generated version constant.
- ObjectReaderCompiler: the debug capture aid (Reflection.Emit's AssemblyBuilderAccess.Save)
  stays .NET Framework only.
- System.Data.SqlClient 4.9.0, the provider the sources name; ILGEN, the way the original
  assembly was built (the materializer per Reflection.Emit).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
